{:edb/db-before-t 785 :edb/db-after-t 786 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534098 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:52:13.417Z" 13194139534098 true] [17592186087671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277519 13194139534098 true] [17592186087671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277526 13194139534098 true] [17592186087672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277533 13194139534098 true] [17592186087672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277540 13194139534098 true] [17592186087999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534098 true] [17592186087999 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nWrite the complex number $z =-1 + 2\\textrm{i}$ in the form $re^{\\textrm{i}θ}$, giving $θ$ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534098 false] [17592186087999 1100 "Write the complex number $z=-1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534098 true] [17592186087999 1145 "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{-1})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-2)| \\\\  & ≈2.034.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =2.034$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.034\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277519 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277520 13194139534098 true] [17592186277519 1089 "q-107428" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277519 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534098 true] [17592186277519 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/ba77669a8e0ffd3e69bfc8e5322d7042c318a55b4cd486ac1fac591d3b016e43.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to the nearest tenth." 13194139534098 true] [17592186277519 1113 #uuid "98e9dda0-b7c6-5b8c-836e-5f373b899981" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277519 1145 "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =2-3\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{3}{2})| \\\\  & ≈5.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\theta =5.3$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277521 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277522 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277523 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277524 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277525 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1041 "selection" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277521 13194139534098 true] [17592186277520 1110 #uuid "d5aad4bf-4ff8-5f2d-bb23-efadfc58c28c" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277521 1034 "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277521 1111 #uuid "90584326-4b33-57bc-80d2-a8018dd5851f" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277522 1034 "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.8\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277522 1111 #uuid "df9c597d-d8ac-56dd-b725-4de35d2a5554" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277523 1034 "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.8\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277523 1111 #uuid "f83c4ac3-3150-5969-922e-65e28006235c" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277524 1034 "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277524 1111 #uuid "ac65ced2-49e1-5c54-afc6-1048b69aae55" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277525 1034 "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.1\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277525 1111 #uuid "0fa4696f-b63e-5d00-9f16-8cf7f8057351" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277526 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277527 13194139534098 true] [17592186277526 1089 "q-17516" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277526 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534098 true] [17592186277526 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/f13d134b7dba012b5b71a7a81ab8071b2706586699b8bf21a6df0d5c44c69619.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534098 true] [17592186277526 1113 #uuid "8cb4fa44-b2a4-5541-ab97-fdfc97dfb573" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277526 1145 "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =3-\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{3})| \\\\  & ≈5.961.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =5.961$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277528 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277529 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277530 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277531 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277532 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1041 "selection" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277531 13194139534098 true] [17592186277527 1110 #uuid "992adc2a-dc98-596d-964a-c8185b3dafc6" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277528 1034 "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277528 1111 #uuid "6bdea5a6-5e6f-5cdb-8c6c-e8a59b1963e9" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277529 1034 "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277529 1111 #uuid "f46e5477-104c-5d20-ad69-057d7a1ebe6a" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277530 1034 "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277530 1111 #uuid "ef4efc0b-98c2-5328-8f70-3b06dbc16ec2" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277531 1034 "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277531 1111 #uuid "4969f735-81fa-557f-a026-c1bc902ef92d" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277532 1034 "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534098 true] [17592186277532 1111 #uuid "ea19fcd0-b18e-55eb-af0f-e9353f15c484" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277533 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277534 13194139534098 true] [17592186277533 1089 "q-8075" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277533 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534098 true] [17592186277533 1100 "Write the complex number $z=1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534098 true] [17592186277533 1113 #uuid "087bd2ce-cf81-51d6-811a-35d764be7f1b" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277533 1145 "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & ≈1.107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =1.107$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277535 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277536 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277537 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277538 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277539 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534098 true] [17592186277534 104